thena spine> :parse LC ( λ x : ι . x )
abs(x, base, var(x))
thena spine> :parse LC (λf:(ι->ι).(λy:ι.f y))
abs(f, arrow(base, base), abs(y, base, app(var(f), var(y))))
thena spine> :parse LC ( λ ? : ι . ? )
abs(?, base, ?)
thena spine> :parse LC f a b
in LC`f a b`: this term parses two ways, as app(var(f), app(var(a), var(b))) and as app(app(var(f), var(a)), var(b))
thena spine> :parse LC { a a }
repeat(var(a), var(a))
thena spine> :parse LC { a b }
in LC`{ a b }`: repeat's M is written more than once and must read the same each time, but here it is var(a) and var(b)
thena spine> :parse LC ( λ x ι )
in LC`( λ x ι )`: unexpected 'ι' at character 7, expecting :
thena spine> :parse LC ( λ x : ι .
in LC`( λ x : ι .`: the term ends too soon, expecting x, ( or {
thena spine> :parse Ty ( ι -> ( ι -> ι ) )
arrow(base, arrow(base, base))
thena spine> :parse Nope x
no language called Nope has been declared
thena spine> :parse LC
each line is an LC term: Tab shows what fits at the cursor, ? is a missing slot, :done leaves
parse LC> ( λ x : ι . x )
abs(x, base, var(x))
parse LC> f a b
in LC`f a b`: this term parses two ways, as app(var(f), app(var(a), var(b))) and as app(app(var(f), var(a)), var(b))
parse LC> :parse LC
in LC`:parse LC`: unexpected ':' at character 1, expecting x, ( or {
parse LC> :done
done parsing LC
thena spine> :parse LC ( λ y : ι . y )
abs(y, base, var(y))
